PracticeFromZecTest
└── fromZec.ask
    ├── given no items
    │   └── it asks nothing
    ├── given a spot rate
    │   ├── it asks which of four things the amount buys
    │   ├── it marks the real item as the correct choice
    │   ├── it moves the answer out of first place
    │   ├── it says what the thing costs in both units
    │   ├── it records which item it asked about
    │   └── it takes the band from the ZEC value
    ├── given a held rate
    │   ├── it prices the question at the held rate
    │   └── given the held rate cannot cover the item's currency
    │       └── it asks nothing
    ├── given no rate for the item's currency
    │   └── it asks nothing
    ├── given a garbage rate
    │   └── it asks nothing
    ├── given an item priced at nothing
    │   └── it asks nothing
    ├── given items priced in different currencies
    │   ├── it prices the item in its own currency
    │   └── it leaves out an item whose currency has no rate
    ├── given a second entry for the same thing
    │   └── it offers the thing once
    ├── given too few items to fill four options
    │   └── it asks nothing
    ├── given a pool clustered inside the narrow separation
    │   └── it asks nothing
    ├── given a pool spanning orders of magnitude
    │   └── it separates every option by an order of magnitude
    ├── given a pool too tight for an order of magnitude
    │   └── it falls back to the narrower separation
    └── given the picker strands the search
        ├── it asks nothing rather than backtracking
        └── it would have found a set from another starting point
